OL,3,GNEWSA'Like bombs going off':
OL,4,AEyewitnesses recall 1986 rail crash
OL,5,
OL,6,FIvy Beresford was in her living room
OL,7,Fone evening in 1986 when she heard a
OL,8,Fdeafening crash.
OL,10,F"It was like two or three bombs going
OL,11,Foff," she says, recalling running to
OL,12,Fthe window to look at the railway line
OL,13,Foutside.
OL,15,F"There was a train heading north and it
OL,16,Fcame to a screeching halt - then
OL,17,Fseconds later another train travelling
OL,18,Fin the opposite direction hit it at
OL,19,Fspeed.
OL,21,F"Then my daughter screamed."
